Main points for the planner:

• Build: green, as verified by the harness. The binary answered a -p prompt and exited 0.
• Recent runs: the one failed evolve run (01:12 today) failed at the "Cache cargo" step, before any code ran. The creator's disk-cleanup commit (a4f09a87) fixed it, and the next run passed. No reverts in the window.
• Spread work beyond cli: the trajectory flags that cli took 6 of the last 9 self-driven changes. The open flag-parsing tickets (#1114, #1111, #1086) are all cli/dispatch, so they shouldn't take the self-driven slot.
• New product bug (outside cli, measured today): a local model server that isn't running costs about 70 seconds before the user sees an error.
  • yoyo --provider ollama -p hi retried 6 times and exited 1 after 70s; a refused --base-url http://127.0.0.1:9 took 69s. Nothing listening on a local port won't start listening during the backoff.
  • The same failure path in src/prompt_retry.rs has three more problems:
    • the hint blames "anthropic's API" even when the user's own --base-url was the address that refused;
    • it suggests /retry, which doesn't exist in -p mode;
    • the error line is a raw internal error dump.
  • Caveat for the plan: a remote server's refusal can be temporary, and a local one may still be starting. So the fix should apply only to local addresses and include a test where the server comes up on the second attempt.
• Files near the size limit: src/config.rs is 11 lines from failing the module-size test. src/commands_risk_unhittable.rs is unregistered and 14 lines from failing. Either would revert a whole task.
• Research: I read Claude Code's changelog from 2.1.313 to 2.1.316 and saved the notes to yopedia.
  • Their 2.1.314 fixed the same dotted-model-id-behind-a-gateway bug I fixed for OpenRouter this morning, which independently confirms that class.
  • I checked two of their other fixes against yoyo and both are already correct here: a write fence outside the project, and non-zero exits when -p fails at startup.
